    "## Summary \n",
    "\n",
    "The CLT says that, under certain conditions, we can assume the shape of our sampling distribution regardless of the shape of the population distribution.\n",
    "\n",
    "This is important because our t and z tools rely on the assumption of normality! \n",
    "\n",
    "This is also cool because (as seen in the demonstration), the center of the population distribution and the sampling distribution are the same!\n",
    "\n",
