    "## Confidence Interval{.smaller} \n",
    "\n",
    "Suppose we want to **estimate** whether the mean home value differs between Wake County and Mecklenburg County. We'll compare 100 homes randomly selected homes in Wake County with 100 randomly selected homes in Mecklenburg County. The Wake County sample had a mean home value of \\$461,300 with a sample standard deviation of \\$120,000, while the Mecklenburg County sample had a mean home value of \\$406,800 with a sample standard deviation of \\$105,000.\n",
    "\n",
    "Let's talk about the intuition behind confidence intervals!\n",
    "\n",
    "## Formula \n",
    "\n",
    "$(\\bar{x}_1-\\bar{x}_2)\\pm t^*\\sqrt{\\frac{s_1^2}{n_1}+\\frac{s_2^2}{n_2}}$\n",
    "\n",
    "$(\\hat{p}_1-\\hat{p}_2)\\pm z^*\\sqrt{\\frac{\\hat{p}_1(1-\\hat{p}_1)}{n_1}+\\frac{\\hat{p}_2(1-\\hat{p}_2)}{n_2}}$\n",
    "\n",
    "## t* \n",
    "\n",
    "$t^*$ is the critical value from the t-distribution that determines how many standard errors we move away from our observed difference in order to capture the desired confidence level.\n",
    "\n",
    "The conservative estimate for our degrees of freedom is $n-1$ of the smaller group!\n",
    "\n",
    "## t* \n",
    "\n",
    "We can find t-star using the following R code... and we know what this value should be close to!\n",
    "\n",
    "```{webr-r}\n",
    "qt(.975, 99, lower.tail = TRUE)\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "## Confidence Interval \n",
    "\n",
    "Calculate a 95% confidence interval\n",
    "\n",
    "## Confidence Interval \n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\begin{aligned}\n",
    "(461{,}300-406{,}800)\n",
    "&\\pm 1.984\\sqrt{\n",
    "\\frac{120{,}000^2}{100}\n",
    "+\n",
    "\\frac{105{,}000^2}{100}\n",
    "}\\\\\n",
    "&=54{,}500\\pm31{,}566\\\\\n",
    "&=\\boxed{(22{,}934,\\ 86{,}066)}\n",
    "\\end{aligned}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
